❌ Common mistakes in older notes (fixed in this file)
1) `@EnableBinding` / `@StreamListener` → legacy; use functional beans
2) Binding name mismatch:
   - Bean `sendOut` expects `sendOut-out-0` (NOT `send-out-0`)
   - Keep bean name and binding name consistent
3) Missing `spring.cloud.function.definition` when multiple functions exist
4) Producer & consumer `destination` must be the same exchange/topic name
5) Forgetting consumer `group` in real microservices


✅ Summary
| Feature     | Traditional AMQP (`RabbitTemplate`) | Spring Cloud Stream              |
| ----------- | ----------------------------------- | -------------------------------- |
| Abstraction | Low-level                           | High-level (binder-based)        |
| API style   | Manual queues / listeners           | Functions + bindings / StreamBridge |
| Ideal for   | Fine-grained AMQP control           | Microservices messaging          |
| Broker swap | Rewrite messaging code              | Often change binder only (Rabbit ↔ Kafka) |
